{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nTask SE-PE-01: Grammar-guided node reduction (Perses-style)\n\nThe algorithm:\n1. Consider nodes in depth-descending order (deeper nodes first), with node ID as stable tiebreaker at equal depth\n2. For each candidate node (removable=True):\n   - Tentatively remove it\n   - Check if all required symbols still remain represented in the remaining tree\n   - If yes, remove it permanently\n   - If no, keep it\n3. Also: never remove root, a required symbol node, or a node with retained children\n\nWait, let me re-read:\n- \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children\"\n- \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\"\n\nSo the constraints are:\n1. Node must be `removable=True`\n2. Node is not root (or rather, root has removable=False)\n3. The node's symbol is not a required symbol - wait, re-reading: \"a required symbol\" - does this mean a node whose symbol is in required_symbols?\n4. The node has no retained children\n5. After removal, all required symbols remain represented\n\nWait, but \"never remove... a required symbol\" - this means don't remove a node whose symbol is in required_symbols. But also \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" - these two constraints seem related.\n\nLet me think again. The required_symbols list specifies symbols that must remain in the tree. So:\n- If a node's symbol is in required_symbols, it cannot be removed (since that would potentially remove coverage of that symbol)\n- Actually: constraint is that all required symbols remain represented after removal\n\nActually constraint 3 (a node with retained children) means: we process depth-descending, so when we consider a parent node, its children may or may not have been removed. If any children are still retained, we can't remove the parent.\n\nLet me re-read: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nSo the hard constraints for removal eligibility:\n1. `removable=True`\n2. Not root (removable=False for root anyway)\n3. Node's symbol is not a required symbol\n4. Node has no retained children\n\nPlus the tentative check:\n5. After tentative removal, all required symbols still have at least one representative in the retained tree\n\nOrder: deeper nodes first, tiebreak by node ID (alphabetically? lexicographically?)\n\nLet me trace through case 0:\n\nNodes:\n- root: depth=0, removable=False, symbol=\"root\"\n- n1: depth=1, removable=False, symbol=\"s1\"\n- n2: depth=1, removable=True, symbol=\"s2\"\n- n3: depth=1, removable=False, symbol=\"s0\"\n- n4: depth=2, removable=True, symbol=\"s1\", parent=n2\n- n5: depth=2, removable=False, symbol=\"s2\", parent=n3\n- n6: depth=2, removable=True, symbol=\"s0\", parent=n1\n\nrequired_symbols = [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nProcessing order (deeper first, then by node ID):\n- Depth 2: n4, n5, n6 (sorted by ID)\n- Depth 1: n1, n2, n3\n- Depth 0: root\n\nFor n4 (depth=2, removable=True, symbol=\"s1\"):\n- Symbol \"s1\" is in required_symbols → cannot remove? \n\nWait, \"never remove... a required symbol\" - does this mean we skip nodes whose symbol is required?\n\nIf we remove n4 (symbol=\"s1\"), we need to check if \"s1\" is still represented. n1 also has symbol=\"s1\" and is not removed, so \"s1\" is still represented. But the rule says \"never remove a required symbol\" - does this mean the symbol itself (node symbol in required_symbols)?\n\nI think the two rules work together:\n- Hard rule: don't remove if symbol is required (to be safe, skip entirely)\n- OR soft rule: try to remove, but check if required symbols still covered\n\nActually, re-reading more carefully: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children\" - this seems to list three types of nodes that cannot be removed. \"A required symbol\" likely means a node whose symbol appears in required_symbols.\n\nBut then \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" - this would be redundant if we already skip required-symbol nodes.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider. Maybe \"a required symbol\" here means the specific root symbol named \"root\" rather than any symbol in required_symbols? Or maybe it means a node that IS required (not removable)?\n\nActually I think the cleaner interpretation is:\n1. Only consider nodes where `removable=True`\n2. Skip nodes that are root\n3. Skip nodes whose symbol is in required_symbols (hard constraint)\n4. Skip nodes that still have retained children (process deep-first helps here)\n5. Even for candidates passing above, tentatively check: if removed, are all required_symbols still represented?\n\nBut wait, with interpretation 3, n4 (symbol=\"s1\") would never be removed. Let me check if that makes sense...\n\nActually, maybe \"a required symbol\" means literally a node that is not removable (i.e., required=True would be the opposite of removable). But the field is named `removable`.\n\nI think the most natural reading is: \n- \"required symbol\" = a node whose symbol is in `required_symbols`\n- Don't remove such nodes\n- Also, tentatively check coverage\n\nBut if n1 has symbol=\"s1\" and is not removable anyway, and n4 has symbol=\"s1\" but is removable... if we never remove nodes with required symbols, we'd keep n4 too.\n\nActually wait, let me reconsider. If we have n1 (symbol=s1, not removable) and n4 (symbol=s1, removable), and required_symbols includes \"s1\", then:\n- The hard rule says don't remove any node with symbol in required_symbols\n- So n4 stays\n\nBUT, the soft rule says \"tentatively remove only if all required symbols remain represented\" - which would also prevent removing n4 if n1 is already gone... but n1 is not removable.\n\nI think both rules together make sense: the hard rule is a quick filter, and the soft rule catches edge cases. Or maybe the hard rule doesn't apply to individual nodes but the soft rule does.\n\nLet me look at it from a different angle. The Perses algorithm works like:\n1. Try to remove a node\n2. If the result is still \"interesting\" (here: all required symbols covered), keep the removal\n3. Otherwise revert\n\nThe \"hard\" constraints about \"never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children\" might be optimization constraints to avoid unnecessary tries.\n\nOK, I think the cleanest implementation is:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case['nodes']\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\n    \n    # Build data structures\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n['id']: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n['parent'] is not None:\n            children[n['parent']].append(n['id'])\n    \n    retained = set(n['id'] for n in nodes)\n    removed_order = []\n    \n    # Sort by depth descending, then by node ID ascending\n    candidates = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\n    \n    for node in candidates:\n        nid = node['id']\n        \n        # Must be removable\n        if not node['removable']:\n            continue\n        \n        # Never remove a node whose symbol is required\n        if node['symbol'] in required_symbols:\n            continue\n        \n        # Must have no retained children\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        # Tentatively remove: check all required symbols still represented\n        tentative = retained - {nid}\n        symbols_present = set(node_map[n]['symbol'] for n in tentative)\n        if not required_symbols.issubset(symbols_present):\n            continue\n        \n        # Remove the node\n        retained = tentative\n        removed_order.append(nid)\n    \n    return {\n        'removed_node_ids': removed_order,\n        'retained_node_ids': sorted(retained)\n    }\n```\n\nWait, but the output says \"Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order.\" So retained_node_ids is sorted, and removed_node_ids is in removal order (not sorted).\n\nLet me trace through case 0:\n\nNodes sorted by (-depth, id):\n- n4: depth=2, id=\"n4\"\n- n5: depth=2, id=\"n5\"  \n- n6: depth=2, id=\"n6\"\n- n1: depth=1, id=\"n1\"\n- n2: depth=1, id=\"n2\"\n- n3: depth=1, id=\"n3\"\n- root: depth=0, id=\"root\"\n\nInitial retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, n6}\n\nProcessing n4:\n- removable=True ✓\n- symbol=\"s1\" is in required_symbols → SKIP\n\nProcessing n5:\n- removable=False → SKIP\n\nProcessing n6:\n- removable=True ✓\n- symbol=\"s0\" not in required_symbols ✓\n- children of n6: none ✓\n- tentative removal: retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5}\n- symbols present: root, s1, s2, s0, s1, s2 → {root, s1, s2, s0}\n- required_symbols = {root, s1} ⊆ {root, s1, s2, s0} ✓\n- REMOVE n6\n- retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5}\n- removed_order = [n6]\n\nProcessing n1:\n- removable=False → SKIP\n\nProcessing n2:\n- removable=True ✓\n- symbol=\"s2\" not in required_symbols ✓\n- children of n2: [n4] - is n4 in retained? Yes → SKIP (has retained children)\n\nProcessing n3:\n- removable=False → SKIP\n\nProcessing root:\n- removable=False → SKIP\n\nFinal:\n- retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5}\n- retained_node_ids sorted: [n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, root]\n- removed_node_ids: [n6]\n\nHmm, this seems correct for case 0. n2 can't be removed because n4 (child) is still retained, and n4 can't be removed because its symbol \"s1\" is required.\n\nLet me verify case 1:\n\nNodes:\n- root: depth=0, removable=False, symbol=\"root\"\n- n1: depth=1, removable=False, symbol=\"s1\"\n- n2: depth=1, removable=True, symbol=\"s2\"\n- n3: depth=1, removable=False, symbol=\"s0\"\n- n4: depth=2, removable=True, symbol=\"s1\", parent=n2\n- n5: depth=2, removable=False, symbol=\"s2\", parent=n3\n- n6: depth=2, removable=True, symbol=\"s0\", parent=n1\n\nrequired_symbols = [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nSame structure as case 0, same result:\n- n4: symbol=\"s1\" → skip\n- n5: not removable → skip\n- n6: removable, s0 not required, no children → check: removing n6, remaining {root,n1,n2,n3,n4,n5}, symbols include root,s1 → remove\n- n1: not removable → skip\n- n2: has retained child n4 → skip\n- n3: not removable → skip\n- root: not removable → skip\n\nremoved_order = [n6]\nretained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5}\n\nCase 2:\nSame structure, same result.\n\nAll three cases seem identical in structure. Let me double-check the retained sort order. The IDs are: root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5 - sorted lexicographically: \"n1\" \u003c \"n2\" \u003c \"n3\" \u003c \"n4\" \u003c \"n5\" \u003c \"root\".\n\nSo retained_node_ids = [\"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\n\nNow let me write the final implementation cleanly:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case['nodes']\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    for n in nodes:\n        for field in ('id', 'parent', 'symbol', 'depth', 'removable'):\n            if field not in n:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Node missing field: {field}\")\n    if 'required_symbols' not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Case missing required_symbols\")\n    \n    # Build lookup structures\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n['id']: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n['parent'] is not None:\n            if n['parent'] not in node_map:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Parent {n['parent']} not found for node {n['id']}\")\n            children[n['parent']].append(n['id'])\n    \n    retained = set(n['id'] for n in nodes)\n    removed_order = []\n    \n    # Process deeper nodes first, tiebreak by node ID ascending\n    candidates = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\n    \n    for node in candidates:\n        nid = node['id']\n        \n        # Only consider removable nodes\n        if not node['removable']:\n            continue\n        \n        # Never remove a node whose symbol is required\n        if node['symbol'] in required_symbols:\n            continue\n        \n        # Never remove a node with retained children\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        # Tentatively remove: verify all required symbols still represented\n        symbols_after = {node_map[n]['symbol'] for n in retained if n != nid}\n        if not required_symbols.issubset(symbols_after):\n            continue\n        \n        # Accept removal\n        retained.discard(nid)\n        removed_order.append(nid)\n    \n    return {\n        'removed_node_ids': removed_order,\n        'retained_node_ids': sorted(retained)\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks good to me. Now I need to encode it as a JSON string in the required envelope format.\n\nThe output must be: `{\"implementation\": \"...python source...\"}` where the python source is JSON-escaped.\n\nLet me write out the implementation as a JSON string, properly escaping newlines and quotes.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = set(case['required_symbols'])\\n\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        for field in ('id', 'parent', 'symbol', 'depth', 'removable'):\\n            if field not in n:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Node missing field: {field}\\\")\\n    if 'required_symbols' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Case missing required_symbols\\\")\\n\\n    # Build lookup structures\\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n['id']: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n['parent'] is not None:\\n            if n['parent'] not in node_map:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Parent {n['parent']} not found for node {n['id']}\\\")\\n            children[n['parent']].append(n['id'])\\n\\n    retained = set(n['id'] for n in nodes)\\n    removed_order = []\\n\\n    # Process deeper nodes first; tiebreak by node ID ascending (lexicographic)\\n    candidates = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n\\n    for node in candidates:\\n        nid = node['id']\\n\\n        # Only consider removable nodes\\n        if not node['removable']:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove a node whose symbol is in required_symbols\\n        if node['symbol'] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove a node that still has retained children\\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Tentatively remove: verify all required symbols remain represented\\n        symbols_after = {node_map[n]['symbol'] for n in retained if n != nid}\\n        if not required_symbols.issubset(symbols_after):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Accept the removal\\n        retained.discard(nid)\\n        removed_order.append(nid)\\n\\n    return {\\n        'removed_node_ids': removed_order,\\n        'retained_node_ids': sorted(retained)\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01ZMyvxyh9V6nQWlhX6u0Nwr","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2553},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2553,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":37,"output_tokens":4127,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3588},"service_tier":"standard"}}